/ Function: A _Function_ $f: A -> B$, wherein $A, B$ are sets, is a _relation_
  $A times B$ that's _functional_, i. e.
  $forall a in A: (a, b_1) in f and (a, b_2) in f ==> b_1 = b_2$
Also, this is very important:
/ Formal Language: A formal Language $L$ over an _alphabet_ (non-empty, finite
  set) $Sigma$ is a subset of $Sigma^*$.

Next, we define something entirely different:

/ Literature: Any utterance of language is considered literature, if it has at
  least one of the following feature:

  + Fixture: The utterance is _fixed_, e. g. by being written down or recorded
  + Fictionality: The utterance is _fictional_
  + Poetic: The utterance uses poetical language

And lastly, this is also very important:
/ Goethe: Johann Wolfgang von Goethe (28 August 1749 – 22 March 1832) was a
  German polymath who is widely regarded as the most influential writer in the
  German language.

This is it.
